    {
      "title": "Women hospitalised and three men charged with assault and choking after separate home invasions in Sydney",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/sydney-home-invasions-arncliffe-bankstown-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>NSW police allege the men, aged 18, 19 and 20, broke into homes in Arncliffe and Bankstown this week before assaulting the women aged 31 and 32</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/02/labor-anthony-albanese-online-gaming-esafety-coalition-angus-taylor-greens-david-shoebridge-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Three men have been detained after two women were allegedly assaulted during separate home invasions in Sydney’s south-west.</p><p>New South Wales police were called to a home invasion in Arncliffe at about midnight on Tuesday morning.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/sydney-home-invasions-arncliffe-bankstown-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T02:34:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon asked police investigator about murder of Lilie James day before shootings, court hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/beau-lamarre-condon-asked-police-investigator-about-of-lilie-james-day-before-shootings-court-hears",
      "description": "<p>Lamarre-Condon asked fellow officer if Paul Thijssen ‘would have gotten away with’ James’s murder if he hadn’t subsequently killed himself</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/02/labor-anthony-albanese-online-gaming-esafety-coalition-angus-taylor-greens-david-shoebridge-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Police officer Beau Lamarre-Condon asked a colleague, a day before he allegedly murdered Jesse Baird and Luke Davies, if a high-profile killer would have “gotten away with it” if he’d not taken his own life, a Sydney court has heard.</p><p>Lamarre-Condon, 31, has been accused of fatally shooting the couple with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/beau-lamarre-condon-asked-police-investigator-about-of-lilie-james-day-before-shootings-court-hears\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T02:04:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Labor targets ‘visa hopping’ international students in crackdown on ‘permanently temporary’ migration",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/labor-migration-crackdown-international-students",
      "description": "<p>Migration agents and lawyers ‘selling false hope’ to people seeking to stay in Australia also in ministers’ sights as they seek to reduce overseas arrivals</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/02/labor-anthony-albanese-online-gaming-esafety-coalition-angus-taylor-greens-david-shoebridge-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>“Visa hopping” international students, migration agents and lawyers trying to “game” the migration system will be targeted by the federal government, as Labor unveils a further crackdown.</p><p>The changes announced on Friday mean international students will soon need to apply for a separate visa to transfer courses, on top of previously announced rules that prevent transferring to a lower grade course, such as switching from a bachelor’s or masters’ degree to a vocational program.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/labor-migration-crackdown-international-students\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T01:33:56"
    }
